At GSUP, I talked with some Presidents of Universities. Most of the Talks were just general affairs. For instants,&ldquo;Where is my seat?&ldquo;or &ldquo;What is the beginning time?&ldquo;and so on. But the following three were interesting exceptions.
One of the president asked me for the toilet.
And I led him to the toilet,&ldquo;go straight and then turn right&rdquo;.
The president behind me said,&ldquo;Please go slowly,young man.&rdquo;
I was embarrassed for going too quickly,because it seemed impolite.
I slowed down my pace and smiled,&ldquo;It is China&rsquo; Pace.&rdquo;
Then I couldn&rsquo;t figure out his facial expression when the president heard my words.
Another President chatted with me.
He came to the reception early and had nothing to do.
&ldquo;Are you from Tsinghua University?&rdquo;
&ldquo;Yeah.&rdquo;
He pointed to my tie,&ldquo;What a lovely tie!It is a Tsinghua Tie or your tie?&rdquo;
&ldquo;Oh, it&rsquo;s mine.&rdquo;
If he had not been a western president but an Arabian , I should send the tie as a present according to his custom.
The third President talked to me.
&ldquo;You are the volunteer from Tsinghua University,yes?&rdquo;
&ldquo;Yes.&rdquo;
&ldquo;What about your major?&rdquo;
&ldquo;My major is aerospace.&rdquo; I answered in a quiet tone.
&ldquo;Aerospace?&ldquo;Obviously,he was surprised,&ldquo;I only know Beihang, does tsinghua has the major?No Kidding?&ldquo;He smiled.
Then I told him that School of Aerospace in Tsinghua was set up in 2004 and developed quickly.
He was satisfied and said ,&ldquo;Thank you.&rdquo;
